{
  "configuration_id": "config_029",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that scvi_n200 dramatically outperforms scgpt as an RNA encoder (config_006: 0.650 acc vs config_018: 0.530 acc, both rna_only/multiprofile/avgpool). The critical open question is whether adding the image modality provides any benefit on top of this already-dominant RNA representation. For scgpt, multimodal did not help in the multiprofile setting (config_009: 0.518 < config_018: 0.530), but scvi_n200 is a fundamentally different learned latent and the interaction is unknown. config_029 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) is the minimal-change extension of config_006: it keeps the same RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation, and only adds the image branch with concat fusion (necessary for two modalities). This directly isolates the marginal contribution of image information given the best RNA encoder. If it matches or exceeds 0.650, image is additive; if it falls below, the scvi_n200 latent already captures what image would contribute, and future budget should focus on RNA-side improvements rather than multimodal fusion."
}

